#!   MARKDOWN_DESCRIPTION="###Description&#10;This transformer checks if input file paths exist and routes features accordingly.&#10;The transformer supports UNC path, Zip files(*.zip) and wildcards. &#10;&#10;###Details&#10;&#10;The transformer will check if the filename selected in InputPort exists or not. &#10;The path can be supplied from a parameter, a network share location, by selecting a filename or using wildcards. &#10;&#10;###Notes&#10;- Multiple filenames are not supported&#10;- Path to file must exist (no missing folders in the path)&#10;- FTP paths are not supported&#10;"
#!   MARKDOWN_USAGE="###Input   &#10;Filename path to check if file exists.   &#10;&#10;###Parameters###&#10;   &#10;###Input ports &#10;**Input File Path**: Full path to the file to check for existence.  &#10;&#10;###Output Ports   &#10;**Exists**:Features are output through this port if the file exists.   &#10;&#10;_\_path:_ The attribute stores the `path` to the file.  &#10;&#10;**DoesNotExist**:Features are output through this port if the file does not exists.   &#10;  &#10;_\_path:_ This attribute stores the `path` to the file.   &#10;"
#!   PYTHON_COMPATIBILITY=""
#!   REPLACED_BY=""
#!   SUPPRESS_UPGRADE="false"
#!   TITLE="FileExistenceChecker"
#!   USAGE="&lt;h3&gt;Input&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Filename path to check if file exists.   &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3&gt;Parameters&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;h3&gt;Input ports&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Input File Path&lt;/strong&gt;: Full path to the file to check for existence.  &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3&gt;Output Ports&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exists&lt;/strong&gt;:Features are output through this port if the file exists.   &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;_path:&lt;/em&gt; The attribute stores the &lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt; to the file.  &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DoesNotExist&lt;/strong&gt;:Features are output through this port if the file does not exists.   &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;_path:&lt;/em&gt; This attribute stores the &lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt; to the file.   &lt;/p&gt;"
